{
  "slug": "speech-writing",
  "concept": "Speech Writing",
  "generated": "2026-09-08",
  "summary": "A speech is built to be heard, not read. The writer's job is to construct sentences that survive the air between the speaker's mouth and the audience's ear — sentences that can be re-listened-to in re",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A speech is built to be heard, not read. The writer's job is to construct sentences that survive the air between the speaker's mouth and the audience's ear - sentences that can be re-listened-to in real time only by the listener's short-term memory.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#overview",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "1. The talk arc (Duarte / Gallo synthesis)",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every well-formed speech has the same five-beat skeleton:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#1-the-talk-arc-duarte-gallo-synthesis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Hook - a sentence, image, statistic, or question that earns the next 30 seconds.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#1-the-talk-arc-duarte-gallo-synthesis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Frame - what this talk is about and why the audience should care. One sentence.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#1-the-talk-arc-duarte-gallo-synthesis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Three acts - the body. The rule of three is not aesthetic; it is cognitive. Three things stay with the audience, five don't.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#1-the-talk-arc-duarte-gallo-synthesis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Turn - the moment where the talk pivots from explanation to implication.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#1-the-talk-arc-duarte-gallo-synthesis",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Call to action - what the audience should do, feel, or remember.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#1-the-talk-arc-duarte-gallo-synthesis",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "2. The 18-minute rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Carmine Gallo's distillation of TED's curation rule: 18 minutes is the ceiling for a focused, memorable single-speaker talk. For longer slots, structure as multiple sub-talks with clear act breaks.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#2-the-18-minute-rule",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "3. The rule of three",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Three is the smallest number that creates a pattern. Use it for:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#3-the-rule-of-three",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Top-level structure (three acts, three stories, three asks)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#3-the-rule-of-three",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Sentence-level lists (\"government of the people, by the people, for the people\")",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#3-the-rule-of-three",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Repeated refrains (Jobs: \"Stay hungry. Stay foolish.\" - repeated three times)",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#3-the-rule-of-three",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "4. Applause-line placement and craft",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Place applause lines at act transitions and the CTA. Never two in a row.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#4-applause-line-placement-and-craft",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "5. Speech reads differently than essay",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Read every draft aloud. If you run out of breath, the sentence is too long.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#5-speech-reads-differently-than-essay",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "6. Stage-direction annotation craft",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Stage directions are inline notes to the speaker about delivery. They live in the delivery script, not the published transcript.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[pause] - short pause, one breath",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[long pause] - full silence, 2–4 seconds",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[lower voice] - drop volume to draw the audience in",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[slow] - drop pace to weight the line",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "[wait for laughter] - explicitly note that the speaker should hold",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Place directions on their own line above the line they modify, in brackets.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#6-stage-direction-annotation-craft",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "7. Trust the audience",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Amateur speeches over-explain. Professional speeches withhold, then resolve.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#7-trust-the-audience",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Tell a story before naming its lesson; let the room reach the conclusion one beat ahead.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#7-trust-the-audience",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use specific detail, not abstraction. \"A blue notebook on the kitchen table\" beats \"a personal object.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#7-trust-the-audience",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Cut your second-best example. Two strong points land harder than three uneven ones.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#7-trust-the-audience",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Don't apologize for the topic, the time slot, or the room.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#7-trust-the-audience",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "8. Ghostwriting ethics",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Capture their voice. Listen to 30+ minutes of their existing speech before drafting.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#8-ghostwriting-ethics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Their stories, not yours. Use anecdotes from their life.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#8-ghostwriting-ethics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "No misattributed lived experience. Never invent a personal anecdote they did not actually experience.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#8-ghostwriting-ethics",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "They get final cut. The speaker must be able to change anything.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#8-ghostwriting-ethics",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Anti-Patterns",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The written-essay-read-aloud. Long sentences, semicolons, nested clauses.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The five-point list. Audiences forget points four and five.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The apology open. \"I'm not really a speaker…\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The unmotivated joke. Humor that doesn't serve the arc.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The buried CTA. Telling the audience what to do in the third-to-last sentence.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Stage directions in the published transcript.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/speech-writing/#anti-patterns",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
